REDBOARD — SAMPLE INPUT FILES
==============================

These three files simulate a real company submitting a decision brief for adversarial review.
The scenario: Ogha Inc is about to launch an AI claims processing system for 12 insurance companies.

HOW TO USE
----------

Step 1 — Open Redboard at http://localhost:8000 and sign in.

Step 2 — Click "New Review" in the sidebar.

Step 3 — STEP 1 (The Proposal):
  Open sample_brief.txt and copy-paste each section into the corresponding form field:
  - PROPOSAL section → Proposal field
  - CONTEXT AND TECHNICAL DETAILS section → Context field
  - OBJECTIVES section → Objectives field

Step 4 — STEP 2 (Company Context):
  From sample_brief.txt:
  - TEAM section → Team field
  - TIMELINE section → Timeline field
  - "50,000 monthly active users across 12 enterprise clients" → User Base
  - "Insurance — auto, homeowner" → Domain
  - "US market" → Geographies
  - "Enterprise insurance companies (B2B)" → User Type
  - TECH STACK section → Tech Stack field
  - STAKEHOLDERS section → Stakeholders field

Step 5 — STEP 3 (Risk & Team):
  From sample_brief.txt:
  - KNOWN RISKS section → Known Risks field
  - REGULATORY ENVIRONMENT section → Regulatory field
  - "Highly Sensitive — financial/medical/legal data" → Data Sensitivity
  - HUMAN OVERSIGHT PLAN section → Human Oversight field
  - ROLLBACK PLAN section → Rollback Plan field
  - SUCCESS METRICS section → Success Metrics field

Step 6 — STEP 4 (Documents):
  Upload BOTH of these files:
  - eval_report.csv (the model evaluation results)
  - architecture_risks.txt (the engineering concerns document)
  
  These files contain critical information the agents WILL find and cite.

Step 7 — Click "LAUNCH ADVERSARIAL PANEL"

WHAT TO EXPECT
--------------
The panel will take 30-90 seconds. It will produce a detailed memo that should:
- Catch the GPT-4o prompt injection risk (from architecture_risks.txt)
- Flag the Azure OpenAI HIPAA/GDPR data processing issue
- Challenge the 91.2% accuracy claim given the biased test set
- Flag the auto-approval path with no secondary review
- Question the July 15 deadline pressure
- Identify the EU AI Act High-Risk classification concern
- Cite specific numbers from the eval report (4.8% false approval rate, 144 incorrect approvals/day)
- Reference the four unresolved rule engine conflicts (RUL-441, RUL-502, RUL-518, RUL-601)

A PDF memo will be emailed to you and available to download.